Hi folks,

I have been wanting to get on this discussion group and the Quantum 
Erasers topic is a splendid opportunity.

Quantum theory and experimental observations (eg., Alain Aspects
experiments in 1964 to test out Bell's Inequality theorem) have given us
indications about the unifying connectedness of the universe. 

Suppose if one were to construct an isolated system (say a mini-universe),
and perform an experiment in this universe. Consider an experiment such as
that of splitting a laser photon into 2 photons. If one measures the
polarization of one of the photons, then the other photon if measured, a
fraction later, or perhaps even instantaneously (if that is possible,
and/or, such a measurement of instantaneity is possible) would have the
complementary polarization. This observation has been made after the
conjecture was first made. The state of polarization of the earlier photon
measured could not have been conveyed to the second photon in short a
short time (by any normal means) given the distance of separation. 

Indeed as Neil Bohr said, the only way if one were to make sense of this
is to accept that the two photons (in spite of being separated by a large
distance) continue to comprise a quantum system. In fact, the photons, 
the observers and the remaining components of the isolated system 
(the mini-universe) together comprise the quantum system. Together, they 
are a unified whole. 

I guess, you must be saying, '....thats all fine, in fact, you reiterated
what we have been talking about.  what are you trying to say, add?....'

Here's what ...

Keep in mind the following .... 

1) The fractal nature of time ( and perhaps, eventual reality).
Mathematician George Cantor was the one to point it out. Time as we know
it, is linear, proceeds along a conceptual straight line. A straight line
has infinitely divisibility .... a Fractal quality. 

2) Space and time together are a SpaceTime continuum (shown by Einstein in
1905, 1915). If time (as we have so far chosen to interpret it) is fractal,
what the heck is space, if not fractal counterpart. 

3) The diffusion equation constructed both in classical and quantum 
mechanics has a physical interpretation that, while signal information may 
travel at the speed limiting that of light, the fact that some event has 
occurred, the disturbance so to speak, is transmitted to the rest of the 
universe instantaneously! Mind Blowing.

4) The Heisenberg's uncertainty principle. There are complementary
qualities of a system, about a system, (popular examples,
position::momentum, energy::time) which cannot simultaneously be measured.
Any measurement of the state of the universe (measurement of the wave
function of the universe) can only be made with so much precision;
precision given perhaps by the smallest of scales where time (and 
space) ceases to preserve or exhibit fractal qualities. 

What am I leading to? .......

The universe is unified and sequential?. 

Any change in the entire universe, occurs one by one. There are no
concurrent events, however smooth events appear to us.  The universe, on
examination on smaller and smaller scales of time, would appear to a
hypothetical observer outside it, as a jerky old movie or a human miming a
robot carrying out its actions sequentially, going from one state to
another. One event is conveyed to the rest of the universe instantaneously
(or, in fractal time) before the next step in evolution of the chaotic
universe is carried out by the universe. 

If you haven't already split your sides laughing out at the notion of the 
universe as a sequential (though, seemingly chaotic) state machine, then 
why don't you send me your criticism of the conjecture.


